WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.027
The phrase data type is often used too broadly.

00:00:03.027 --> 00:00:05.792
In this course, we separate four layers.

00:00:05.792 --> 00:00:09.137
Data organization describes the form of the dataset.

00:00:09.137 --> 00:00:14.112
Measurement scale describes the meaning of one variable.

00:00:14.112 --> 00:00:19.862
Numeric behavior asks whether a quantitative concept comes from counting or measuring.

00:00:19.862 --> 00:00:25.282
Technical representation describes how software stores the value.

00:00:25.282 --> 00:00:31.147
A single variable can have an answer at several layers, and those answers are not interchangeable.

00:00:31.147 --> 00:00:36.187
Connect this idea to an e-commerce team preparing customer, purchase, and web-event data.

00:00:36.187 --> 00:00:42.007
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:42.007 --> 00:00:48.727
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:48.727 --> 00:00:55.717
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:55.717 --> 00:01:00.480
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
